# `src/lib` utility folders

Each **utility** lives in its own directory: `src/lib/<util-name>/`.

## Required layout

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.ts` | **Public API** — re-export what other code may import. App and feature code import only from `lib/<util-name>` (this barrel). |
| `<util-name>.ts` | Implementation (and internal helpers not meant for consumers). |
| `<util-name>.test.ts` | Tests for the util. |

Use **kebab-case** for `<util-name>` (folder and `.ts` basename match).

## Imports

- **Consumers** (e.g. `popup.ts`, `background.ts`): `import { thing } from "./lib/<util-name>";`
- **Do not** deep-import `./lib/<util-name>/<util-name>.ts` from app code.
- **Tests** should prefer the **barrel** (`./index`) when asserting the public surface. Import from `./<util-name>` only when testing implementation details or symbols intentionally not re-exported from `index.ts`.

## Test-only or internal exports

Keep implementation-only symbols in `<util-name>.ts`. If tests need them without widening the public API for the app:

- Re-export from `index.ts` with a short comment (e.g. test-only helper), **or**
- Import from `./<util-name>` in `*.test.ts` only (white-box tests).

Do not add a second barrel; `index.ts` remains the single external interface for the util package.

## Example

```
src/lib/escape-html/
  index.ts           → export { escapeHtml } from "./escape-html";
  escape-html.ts
  escape-html.test.ts
```
